<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="UTF-8" />
<title>{{ state_name }} — Family Court Data Report</title>
<link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com">
<link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.gstatic.com" crossorigin>
<link rel="stylesheet" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Oswald:wght@400;500;600;700&family=Fraunces:ital,opsz,wght@0,9..144,400;0,9..144,600;1,9..144,400;1,9..144,600&family=Inter:wght@400;500;600;700;800&display=swap">
<style>
  :root {
    --navy: #0F1E30;
    --navy-panel: #1E3A5F;
    --gold: #C9A227;
    --crimson: #B91C1C;
    --ink: #111827;
    --ink-muted: #4B5563;
    --page-bg: #F8F5EE;
    --hairline: rgba(15,30,48,0.15);
    --hairline-strong: rgba(15,30,48,0.35);
    --font-display: 'Oswald', 'Arial Narrow', sans-serif;
    --font-editorial: 'Fraunces', Georgia, serif;
    --font-body: 'Inter', -apple-system, sans-serif;
  }
  * { box-sizing: border-box; }
  html, body { margin: 0; padding: 0; background: #e5e5e5; }
  body { font-family: var(--font-body); color: var(--ink); line-height: 1.5; }

  .page {
    width: 8.5in;
    min-height: 11in;
    background: var(--page-bg);
    margin: 24px auto;
    padding: 0.6in 0.65in 0.85in;
    position: relative;
    box-shadow: 0 2px 8px rgba(0,0,0,0.15);
    overflow: hidden;
  }
  .page::before {
    content: "";
    position: absolute;
    top: 0; left: 0; right: 0;
    height: 6px;
    background: var(--gold);
  }
  .runhead {
    display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: baseline;
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.14em;
    font-size: 10px;
    color: var(--navy);
    padding-bottom: 10px;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--hairline);
    margin-bottom: 22px;
  }
  .runhead .r-state { color: var(--crimson); font-weight: 700; }
  .runhead .r-page { opacity: 0.55; }

  .eyebrow {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.16em;
    color: var(--crimson);
    font-weight: 600;
    font-size: 11px;
  }
  .display {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: -0.01em;
    line-height: 0.92;
    color: var(--navy);
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }
  .section-head {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    font-weight: 600;
    font-size: 13px;
    color: var(--crimson);
    padding-bottom: 8px;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--hairline-strong);
    margin: 28px 0 18px;
  }
  .subsection {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.16em;
    font-size: 10px;
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--gold);
    margin: 16px 0 6px;
    padding-bottom: 4px;
    border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(201,162,39,0.35);
  }
  .subsection:first-of-type { margin-top: 8px; }
  .section-head .num {
    display: inline-block;
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    background: var(--crimson);
    color: #fff;
    padding: 2px 8px;
    margin-right: 10px;
    font-weight: 700;
  }
  .lede {
    font-family: var(--font-editorial);
    font-size: 15.5px;
    line-height: 1.55;
    color: var(--ink);
  }
  .body-text {
    font-size: 12.5px;
    color: var(--ink);
    line-height: 1.55;
  }
  .caption {
    font-size: 10.5px;
    color: var(--ink-muted);
    line-height: 1.45;
  }

  /* COVER */
  .cover { padding: 0; background: var(--navy); color: #fff; overflow: hidden; }
  .cover::before { z-index: 5; }
  .cover-banner-img { display: none; }
  .cover-photo-col { display: none; }
  .cover-inner {
    position: relative;
    padding: 0.85in 0.75in 0.7in;
    min-height: 11in;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    justify-content: space-between;
    z-index: 3;
  }
  .cover-portrait {
    position: absolute;
    inset: 0;
    background-image: url('../assets/meg-no-words-web.jpg');
    background-size: cover;
    background-position: center 22%;
    z-index: 1;
  }
  .cover-portrait::after {
    content: "";
    position: absolute;
    inset: 0;
    background: linear-gradient(180deg, rgba(15,30,48,0.55) 0%, rgba(15,30,48,0.2) 35%, rgba(15,30,48,0.65) 72%, rgba(15,30,48,0.95) 100%);
  }
  .cover-inner > * { position: relative; z-index: 3; }

  body[data-cover="split"] .cover-portrait { display: none; }
  body[data-cover="split"] .cover {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1.05fr 0.95fr;
    grid-template-rows: 1fr;
  }
  body[data-cover="split"] .cover-inner {
    padding: 0.75in 0.55in 0.6in 0.75in;
    min-height: 11in;
  }
  body[data-cover="split"] .cover-photo-col {
    display: block;
    position: relative;
    background-image: url('../assets/meg-no-words-web.jpg');
    background-size: cover;
    background-position: 55% 30%;
    border-left: 4px solid var(--gold);
  }
  body[data-cover="split"] .cover-photo-col::after {
    content: "";
    position: absolute; inset: 0;
    background: linear-gradient(180deg, rgba(15,30,48,0.08) 0%, rgba(15,30,48,0.0) 40%, rgba(15,30,48,0.55) 100%);
  }
  body[data-cover="split"] .cover-photo-col .caption {
    position: absolute; left: 20px; right: 20px; bottom: 20px;
    font-family: var(--font-display); text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.14em; font-size: 10px; color: var(--gold);
    padding-top: 10px; border-top: 1px solid rgba(201,162,39,0.5);
    z-index: 2;
  }
  body[data-cover="split"] .cover-photo-col .caption strong { color: #fff; display: block; font-family: var(--font-editorial); font-style: italic; font-weight: 400; text-transform: none; letter-spacing: 0; font-size: 13px; margin-top: 4px; }
  body[data-cover="split"] .cover h1 { font-size: 92px; }
  body[data-cover="split"] .cover h1 .state-accent { font-size: 54px; }

  body[data-cover="banner"] .cover-portrait { display: none; }
  body[data-cover="banner"] .cover { background: var(--navy); color: #fff; }
  body[data-cover="banner"] .cover-banner-img {
    display: block;
    height: 4.2in;
    background-image: url('../assets/meg-with-words-web.jpg');
    background-size: contain;
    background-position: center center;
    background-repeat: no-repeat;
    background-color: var(--navy);
    position: relative;
    border-bottom: 6px solid var(--crimson);
  }
  body[data-cover="banner"] .cover-banner-img::after {
    content: ""; position: absolute; inset: 0;
    background: linear-gradient(180deg, rgba(15,30,48,0) 55%, rgba(15,30,48,0.7) 100%);
  }
  body[data-cover="banner"] .cover-banner-img .banner-brand { display: none; }
  body[data-cover="banner"] .cover-banner-img .banner-brand-alt { display: none; }
  body[data-cover="banner"] .cover {
    background: var(--navy);
    color: #fff;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
  }
  body[data-cover="banner"] .cover-inner {
    padding: 0.55in 0.75in 0.7in;
    min-height: 0;
    flex: 1;
    color: #fff;
  }
  body[data-cover="banner"] .cover h1 { color: #fff; font-size: 88px; margin-top: 12px; }
  body[data-cover="banner"] .cover h1 .state-accent { color: var(--gold); font-size: 48px; margin-top: 6px; }
  body[data-cover="banner"] .cover .tagline { color: rgba(255,255,255,0.88); text-shadow: none; }
  body[data-cover="banner"] .cover .cover-eyebrow { color: var(--gold); }
  body[data-cover="banner"] .cover .key-figure { color: #fff; border-color: rgba(255,255,255,0.2); }
  body[data-cover="banner"] .cover .key-figure .num { color: var(--gold); }
  body[data-cover="banner"] .cover .key-figure .desc { color: rgba(255,255,255,0.75); }
  body[data-cover="banner"] .cover .meta { color: rgba(255,255,255,0.7); border-top-color: rgba(255,255,255,0.2); }
  body[data-cover="banner"] .cover .meta-item strong { color: #fff; }
  body[data-cover="banner"] .cover .gold-rule { background: var(--gold); }
  body[data-cover="banner"] .cover .brand-mark { display: none; }
  .cover .brand-mark {
    display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 14px;
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.16em;
  }
  .cover .brand-mark .chip {
    background: var(--crimson);
    width: 32px; height: 32px;
    display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center;
    font-weight: 700; font-size: 16px;
  }
  .cover .brand-mark .wordmark { font-weight: 700; font-size: 14px; letter-spacing: 0.18em; }
  .cover .brand-mark .sub { color: var(--gold); font-size: 11px; font-weight: 500; }

  .cover-eyebrow {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.2em;
    font-size: 12px;
    color: var(--gold);
    font-weight: 500;
  }
  .cover h1 {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-weight: 700;
    font-size: 118px;
    line-height: 0.86;
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
    color: #fff;
    margin: 18px 0 0;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    text-shadow: 0 4px 20px rgba(0,0,0,0.4);
  }
  .cover h1 .state-accent { display: block; color: var(--gold); font-size: 78px; line-height: 0.95; margin-top: 10px; letter-spacing: 0.01em; }
  .cover .tagline {
    font-family: var(--font-editorial);
    font-size: 19px;
    font-style: italic;
    line-height: 1.4;
    color: rgba(255,255,255,0.92);
    max-width: 520px;
    margin: 26px 0 0;
    text-shadow: 0 2px 12px rgba(0,0,0,0.5);
  }
  .cover .gold-rule { width: 60px; height: 3px; background: var(--gold); margin: 26px 0; }
  .cover .key-figure {
    display: flex;
    align-items: baseline;
    gap: 18px;
    margin-top: 32px;
  }
  .cover .key-figure .num {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-weight: 700;
    font-size: 96px;
    color: var(--gold);
    line-height: 0.9;
  }
  .cover .key-figure .desc {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.1em;
    font-size: 13px;
    color: rgba(255,255,255,0.75);
    line-height: 1.3;
    max-width: 220px;
  }
  .cover .meta {
    display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: flex-end;
    gap: 32px;
    padding-top: 32px;
    border-top: 1px solid rgba(201,162,39,0.3);
  }
  .cover .meta-item {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.12em;
    font-size: 10px;
    color: rgba(255,255,255,0.55);
  }
  .cover .meta-item strong {
    display: block;
    color: #fff;
    font-size: 14px;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    margin-top: 4px;
    font-weight: 600;
  }

  /* STAT ROWS */
  .headline-stats {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(4, 1fr);
    gap: 0;
    margin: 20px 0 0;
    border-top: 2px solid var(--navy);
    border-bottom: 2px solid var(--navy);
  }
  .hstat {
    padding: 18px 14px;
    border-right: 1px solid var(--hairline);
  }
  .hstat:last-child { border-right: none; }
  .hstat .label {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.1em;
    font-size: 9.5px;
    color: var(--crimson);
    font-weight: 600;
    margin-bottom: 6px;
  }
  .hstat .value {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: 42px;
    font-weight: 700;
    line-height: 0.95;
    color: var(--navy);
    letter-spacing: -0.01em;
  }
  .hstat .value.red { color: var(--crimson); }
  .hstat .note { margin-top: 6px; font-size: 10px; color: var(--ink-muted); line-height: 1.35; }

  /* SECONDARY STATS */
  .secondary-stats {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(4, 1fr);
    gap: 10px;
    margin: -2px 0 14px;
  }
  .sstat {
    background: #fff;
    border: 1px solid var(--hairline);
    padding: 12px 14px;
  }
  .sstat .label {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    font-size: 9px;
    color: var(--ink-muted);
  }
  .sstat .value {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: 22px;
    font-weight: 700;
    color: var(--navy);
    line-height: 1.1;
    margin-top: 4px;
  }

  /* CHART / DATA SECTIONS */
  .data-block { margin-bottom: 18px; }
  .data-block h3 {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.09em;
    font-weight: 600;
    font-size: 12px;
    color: var(--navy);
    margin: 0 0 4px;
    padding-bottom: 6px;
    border-bottom: 2px solid var(--navy);
    display: flex;
    justify-content: space-between;
    align-items: baseline;
  }
  .data-block h3 .chart-meta {
    font-family: var(--font-body);
    text-transform: none;
    letter-spacing: 0;
    font-weight: 500;
    font-size: 9px;
    color: var(--ink-muted);
  }
  .chart-axis {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 180px 1fr 44px 40px;
    gap: 10px;
    align-items: center;
    padding: 3px 0 0;
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: 8px;
    color: var(--ink-muted);
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.1em;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--hairline);
    margin-bottom: 2px;
  }
  .grid-2 .chart-axis { grid-template-columns: 120px 1fr 34px 34px; gap: 8px; }
  .chart-axis .axis-scale { position: relative; height: 10px; }
  .chart-axis .axis-scale::before,
  .chart-axis .axis-scale::after {
    content: attr(data-min);
    position: absolute;
    bottom: 0;
    left: 0;
  }
  .chart-axis .axis-scale::after {
    content: attr(data-max);
    left: auto; right: 0;
  }
  .chart-axis .axis-scale .mid {
    position: absolute;
    left: 50%;
    transform: translateX(-50%);
    bottom: 0;
    color: rgba(15,30,48,0.35);
  }

  .bar-row {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 180px 1fr 44px 40px;
    gap: 10px;
    align-items: center;
    padding: 6px 0;
    font-size: 11px;
    border-bottom: 1px dotted rgba(15,30,48,0.12);
  }
  .grid-2 .bar-row {
    grid-template-columns: 150px 1fr 34px 34px;
    gap: 8px;
  }
  .grid-2 .bar-row .bar-label { font-size: 10px; }
  .bar-row:last-child { border-bottom: none; }
  .bar-row .bar-label {
    color: var(--ink);
    font-weight: 500;
    overflow: visible;
    text-overflow: clip;
    white-space: normal;
    line-height: 1.2;
    font-size: 10.5px;
  }
  .bar-row .bar-track {
    height: 12px;
    background: transparent;
    position: relative;
    border-left: 1px solid rgba(15,30,48,0.3);
  }
  .bar-row .bar-track::before {
    content: "";
    position: absolute;
    inset: 0;
    background-image:
      linear-gradient(to right, transparent 24.75%, rgba(15,30,48,0.08) 24.75%, rgba(15,30,48,0.08) 25.25%, transparent 25.25%),
      linear-gradient(to right, transparent 49.75%, rgba(15,30,48,0.18) 49.75%, rgba(15,30,48,0.18) 50.25%, transparent 50.25%),
      linear-gradient(to right, transparent 74.75%, rgba(15,30,48,0.08) 74.75%, rgba(15,30,48,0.08) 75.25%, transparent 75.25%);
    pointer-events: none;
  }
  .bar-row .bar-fill {
    height: 100%;
    background: var(--navy);
    position: relative;
  }
  .bar-row .bar-fill.is-alert { background: var(--crimson); }
  .bar-row .bar-fill.is-accent { background: var(--gold); }
  .bar-row .bar-fill::after {
    content: "";
    position: absolute;
    right: 0; top: 0; bottom: 0;
    width: 2px;
    background: rgba(0,0,0,0.25);
  }
  .bar-row .bar-count {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-weight: 600;
    font-size: 13px;
    text-align: right;
    color: var(--navy);
    letter-spacing: -0.01em;
  }
  .bar-row .bar-pct {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-weight: 700;
    font-size: 11px;
    text-align: right;
    color: var(--crimson);
    letter-spacing: 0.02em;
  }
  .chart-footer {
    margin-top: 6px;
    padding-top: 6px;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--hairline);
    font-family: var(--font-editorial);
    font-style: italic;
    font-size: 10px;
    color: var(--ink-muted);
    line-height: 1.4;
  }

  .grid-2 { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: 22px; }

  /* EXPENSE TABLE */
  .expense-table { width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; font-size: 11px; }
  .expense-table thead th {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    font-size: 9.5px;
    color: var(--crimson);
    text-align: left;
    padding: 8px 8px;
    border-bottom: 2px solid var(--navy);
    font-weight: 600;
  }
  .expense-table thead th.num { text-align: right; }
  .expense-table tbody td {
    padding: 9px 8px;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--hairline);
    color: var(--ink);
    font-size: 11px;
  }
  .expense-table tbody td.num { text-align: right; font-family: var(--font-display); font-weight: 600; }
  .expense-table tbody td.headline { font-weight: 600; color: var(--navy); }
  .expense-table tbody tr.total-row td {
    border-top: 2px solid var(--navy);
    border-bottom: none;
    font-weight: 700;
    color: var(--navy);
    padding-top: 12px;
  }
  .footnote-marker {
    display: inline-block;
    background: var(--crimson);
    color: #fff;
    font-size: 9px;
    font-weight: 700;
    padding: 1px 5px;
    margin-left: 6px;
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    vertical-align: super;
    letter-spacing: 0.02em;
    border-radius: 2px;
  }
  .footnote {
    margin-top: 14px;
    padding: 10px 14px;
    background: rgba(201,162,39,0.08);
    border-left: 3px solid var(--gold);
    font-size: 10px;
    color: var(--ink-muted);
    line-height: 1.55;
  }
  .footnote strong { color: var(--navy); }


  .actor-table {
    margin-top: 18px;
    border-top: 2px solid var(--navy);
    border-bottom: 2px solid var(--navy);
  }
  .actor-row {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1.35fr 0.9fr 1.05fr 76px;
    gap: 14px;
    align-items: center;
    padding: 10px 8px;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--hairline);
    font-size: 11px;
  }
  .actor-row:last-child { border-bottom: none; }
  .actor-row.header {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    font-size: 9.5px;
    color: var(--crimson);
    font-weight: 600;
    padding-top: 8px;
    padding-bottom: 8px;
  }
  .actor-name { font-weight: 700; color: var(--navy); }
  .actor-count {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-weight: 700;
    color: var(--crimson);
    text-align: right;
    white-space: nowrap;
  }

  /* COURT ACTOR CARDS — name, role, county header + anonymized family comments below */
  .actor-cards { margin-top: 14px; }
  .actor-card {
    border-top: 1px solid var(--hairline);
    padding: 14px 0 12px;
    page-break-inside: avoid;
  }
  .actor-card:first-child {
    border-top: 2px solid var(--navy);
    padding-top: 14px;
  }
  .actor-card:last-child {
    border-bottom: 2px solid var(--navy);
    padding-bottom: 14px;
  }
  .actor-card-header {
    display: flex;
    justify-content: space-between;
    align-items: baseline;
    gap: 12px;
    margin-bottom: 8px;
  }
  .actor-card-header .name {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: 15px;
    font-weight: 700;
    color: var(--navy);
    letter-spacing: -0.005em;
  }
  .actor-card-header .meta {
    font-size: 9.5px;
    color: var(--ink-secondary, #555);
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.07em;
    text-align: right;
    flex-shrink: 0;
  }
  .actor-card-header .meta .families {
    color: var(--crimson);
    font-weight: 700;
  }
  .actor-comments {
    list-style: none;
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
  }
  .actor-comments li {
    font-size: 10.5px;
    line-height: 1.55;
    color: #2a2a2a;
    padding: 4px 0 4px 12px;
    margin-bottom: 4px;
    border-left: 2px solid var(--hairline);
  }
  .actor-comments li:last-child { margin-bottom: 0; }
  .actor-comments .comment-text {
    font-style: italic;
    color: #1a1a1a;
  }
  .actor-comments .comment-county {
    display: inline-block;
    margin-left: 6px;
    font-style: normal;
    font-size: 9px;
    color: var(--crimson);
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.06em;
    font-weight: 600;
  }

  /* PULL QUOTE / VOICES */
  .pullquote {
    background: var(--navy);
    color: #fff;
    padding: 22px 30px 20px;
    margin: 10px 0 14px;
    position: relative;
  }
  .pullquote::before {
    content: "";
    position: absolute;
    left: 0; top: 0; bottom: 0;
    width: 6px;
    background: var(--gold);
  }
  .pullquote .mark {
    font-family: var(--font-editorial);
    font-size: 64px;
    line-height: 0.5;
    color: var(--gold);
    margin-bottom: 6px;
    display: block;
    height: 28px;
  }
  .pullquote blockquote {
    margin: 0;
    font-family: var(--font-editorial);
    font-style: italic;
    font-size: 17px;
    line-height: 1.3;
    color: #fff;
    letter-spacing: -0.005em;
  }
  .pullquote cite {
    display: block;
    margin-top: 10px;
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-style: normal;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.12em;
    font-size: 10px;
    color: var(--gold);
  }

  .voice-card {
    padding: 11px 14px 11px 16px;
    background: #fff;
    border-left: 3px solid var(--gold);
    margin-bottom: 8px;
    position: relative;
  }
  .voice-card blockquote {
    margin: 0;
    font-family: var(--font-editorial);
    font-size: 12px;
    line-height: 1.45;
    color: var(--ink);
  }
  .voice-card cite {
    display: block;
    margin-top: 6px;
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-style: normal;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.1em;
    font-size: 9px;
    color: var(--crimson);
    font-weight: 600;
  }

  .full-comments-list {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 10px;
  }
  .full-comment-card {
    background: #fff;
    border-left: 3px solid var(--gold);
    padding: 10px 12px 9px;
    break-inside: avoid;
  }
  .full-comment-card blockquote {
    margin: 0;
    font-family: var(--font-editorial);
    font-size: 11.2px;
    line-height: 1.42;
    color: var(--ink);
  }
  .full-comment-card cite {
    display: block;
    margin-top: 7px;
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.10em;
    font-size: 8px;
    color: var(--crimson);
    font-weight: 700;
    font-style: normal;
  }

  .voices-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
    gap: 8px;
  }

  /* METHODOLOGY */
  .methodology {
    background: var(--navy);
    color: #fff;
    padding: 24px 28px;
    margin-top: 22px;
  }
  .methodology h3 {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.12em;
    font-size: 11px;
    color: var(--gold);
    margin: 0 0 10px;
  }
  .methodology p {
    font-size: 11px;
    line-height: 1.6;
    margin: 0 0 8px;
    color: rgba(255,255,255,0.8);
  }
  .methodology p:last-child { margin-bottom: 0; }
  .methodology .site {
    margin-top: 14px;
    padding-top: 14px;
    border-top: 1px solid rgba(201,162,39,0.3);
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.14em;
    font-size: 10px;
    color: var(--gold);
  }

  /* MEG'S STORY */
  .megs-story {
    display: block;
    margin: 20px 0 8px;
    background: var(--navy);
    color: #fff;
    border-top: 4px solid var(--crimson);
  }
  .megs-story .story-text { padding: 22px 26px; }
  .megs-story .story-text h3 {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-weight: 700;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    font-size: 26px;
    line-height: 0.95;
    color: #fff;
    margin: 0 0 10px;
  }
  .megs-story .story-text h3 .accent { color: var(--gold); }
  .megs-story .story-text .lede {
    font-family: var(--font-editorial);
    font-size: 12.5px;
    line-height: 1.55;
    color: rgba(255,255,255,0.9);
    margin: 0 0 10px;
  }
  .megs-story .story-text .bullets {
    list-style: none;
    margin: 6px 0 12px;
    padding: 0;
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-weight: 700;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.04em;
    font-size: 12px;
    color: var(--crimson);
  }
  .megs-story .story-text .bullets li { padding: 2px 0 2px 14px; position: relative; }
  .megs-story .story-text .bullets li::before { content: "■"; position: absolute; left: 0; color: var(--crimson); }
  .megs-story .story-text .divider { height: 1px; background: rgba(201,162,39,0.4); margin: 10px 0; }
  .megs-story .story-text p {
    font-family: var(--font-editorial);
    font-size: 12px;
    line-height: 1.55;
    color: rgba(255,255,255,0.86);
    margin: 0;
  }
  .megs-story .story-text .signoff {
    margin-top: 12px;
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.12em;
    font-size: 10px;
    color: var(--gold);
  }
  .megs-story .story-photo {
    background-image: url('../assets/meg-family-only-web.jpg');
    background-size: cover;
    background-position: center center;
    min-height: 340px;
  }

  /* PAGE FOOTER */
  .page-foot {
    position: absolute;
    left: 0.65in; right: 0.65in; bottom: 0.32in;
    display: flex;
    justify-content: space-between;
    align-items: center;
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.12em;
    font-size: 9px;
    color: var(--ink-muted);
    padding-top: 8px;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--hairline);
  }
  .page-foot .credit { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 8px; }
  .page-foot .credit .star {
    display: inline-flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center;
    width: 16px; height: 16px; background: var(--crimson); color: #fff;
    font-size: 10px; font-weight: 700;
  }
  .page-foot .credit strong { color: var(--crimson); font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: 0.08em; }
  .page-foot .pg { color: var(--navy); font-weight: 700; }

  @media print {
    body { background: #fff; }
    .page { margin: 0; box-shadow: none; width: 100%; min-height: 11in; height: 11in; padding: 0.5in 0.5in 0.7in; break-after: page; page-break-after: always; overflow: hidden; }
    .page:last-child { break-after: auto; page-break-after: auto; }
    @page { size: letter; margin: 0; }
    .cover { padding: 0; min-height: 11in; height: 11in; }
  }
</style>
</head>
<body data-cover="banner">

{# ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━ PAGE 1 — COVER ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━ #}
<section class="page cover">
  <div class="cover-portrait"></div>

  <div class="cover-banner-img" style="font-weight: 300;">
    <div class="banner-brand">
      <div>
        <div class="wordmark" style="font-family: var(--font-display); text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.02em; font-weight: 600; font-size: 20px;">Stand<span style="color: #fca5a5;">With</span>Meg.com</div>
        <div class="sub" style="font-family: var(--font-display); text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.2em;">Family Rights Registry</div>
      </div>
      <div class="right-meta">State Series · No. {{ state_number }}</div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="cover-inner">
    <div>
      <div class="brand-mark">
        <div class="chip">★</div>
        <div>
          <div class="wordmark">Stand<span style="color: var(--crimson);">With</span>Meg.com</div>
          <div class="sub">Family Rights Registry</div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div>
        <div class="cover-eyebrow">Family Court Data Report · State Series · No. {{ state_number }}</div>
        <h1>{{ state_name }}<span class="state-accent">what families are reporting.</span></h1>
        <p class="tagline">Pulled from the Family Rights Registry — the first cross-state dataset on what pro se parents are actually experiencing inside {{ state_name }}'s family courts and child-welfare system.</p>
        <div class="gold-rule"></div>

        <div class="key-figure">
          <div class="num">{{ total }}</div>
          <div class="desc">{{ state_name }} families on record · {{ children_total }} children impacted · {{ months_lost_median }} {% if months_lost_median == 1 %}month{% else %}months{% endif %} median months lost of parenting time</div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="meta">
      <div class="meta-item">Report generated<strong>{{ report_date }}</strong></div>
      <div class="meta-item">Counties represented<strong>{{ counties_represented }} of {{ counties_in_state }}</strong></div>
      <div class="meta-item">Compiled by<strong>Meg · standwithmeg.com</strong></div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="cover-photo-col">
    <div class="caption">
      Compiled by
      <strong>Meg · founder, standwithmeg.com</strong>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

{# ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━ NAMED COURT ACTORS — paginates across multiple pages ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━ #}
{% for actor_page in actor_pages %}
{% set this_page_number = actor_start_page + loop.index0 %}
<section class="page">
  <div class="runhead">
    <div><span class="r-state">{{ state_name }}</span> · Family Court Data Report</div>
    <div class="r-page">Stand With Meg · {{ "%02d"|format(this_page_number) }} / {{ total_pages }}</div>
  </div>

  {% if loop.first %}
  <h2 class="section-head"><span class="num">{{ actor_section_num }}</span>Named Court Actors · {{ state_name }}</h2>
  <p class="lede" style="margin-bottom: 18px;">A name appears below only after {{ court_actor_threshold }} or more independent families have named the same actor in {{ state_name }}. Submitter names, emails, and contact details are never published. Comments below are direct family reports — one per family — with all identifying information removed.</p>
  {% else %}
  <h2 class="section-head"><span class="num">{{ actor_section_num }}</span>Named Court Actors, continued</h2>
  {% endif %}

  <div class="actor-cards">
    {% for actor in actor_page %}
    <div class="actor-card">
      <div class="actor-card-header">
        <div class="name">{{ actor.name }}</div>
        <div class="meta">
          {{ actor.role }}{% if actor.court_or_county %} · {{ actor.court_or_county }}{% endif %} · <span class="families">{{ actor.count }} {% if actor.count == 1 %}family{% else %}families{% endif %}</span>
        </div>
      </div>
      {% if actor.comments %}
      <ul class="actor-comments">
        {% for c in actor.comments %}
        <li>
          <span class="comment-text">"{{ c.note }}"</span>
          {% if c.court_or_county and c.court_or_county != actor.court_or_county %}<span class="comment-county">{{ c.court_or_county }}</span>{% endif %}
        </li>
        {% endfor %}
      </ul>
      {% endif %}
    </div>
    {% endfor %}
  </div>

  {% if loop.last %}
  <div class="footnote" style="margin-top: 16px;">
    <strong>Public threshold rule:</strong> Names are grouped conservatively by normalized spelling, role, and location. Common titles, punctuation, casing, and middle initials collapse together. Close misspellings are not auto-merged without admin review. Only family-direct submissions count toward the public threshold.
  </div>
  {% endif %}

  <div class="page-foot">
    <div class="credit"><span class="star">★</span><span>A <strong>StandWithMeg.com</strong> Report · Family Rights Registry</span></div>
    <div class="pg">{{ state_name }} · {{ "%02d"|format(this_page_number) }} / {{ total_pages }}</div>
  </div>
</section>
{% endfor %}

{# ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━ AT A GLANCE ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━ #}
<section class="page">
  <div class="runhead">
    <div><span class="r-state">{{ state_name }}</span> · Family Court Data Report</div>
    <div class="r-page">Stand With Meg · {{ "%02d"|format(glance_page_number) }} / {{ total_pages }}</div>
  </div>

  <div class="eyebrow">The Headline Numbers</div>
  <div class="display" style="font-size: 44px; margin: 10px 0 18px;">{{ state_name }} at a glance.</div>
  <p class="lede">Across {{ total }} {{ state_name }} families reporting through the Family Rights Registry, the patterns are consistent: long durations in court, serious financial loss, and a disproportionate number of parents going unrepresented because they ran out of money fighting.</p>

  <div class="headline-stats">
    <div class="hstat">
      <div class="label">Children Impacted</div>
      <div class="value">{{ children_total }}</div>
      <div class="note">{{ children_reporting }} of {{ total }} families reported child counts</div>
    </div>
    <div class="hstat">
      <div class="label">Estimated Family Impact</div>
      <div class="value red">{{ median_family_impact }}</div>
      <div class="note">sum of median reported expenses</div>
    </div>
    <div class="hstat">
      <div class="label">Median Months Lost</div>
      <div class="value">{{ months_lost_median }}</div>
      <div class="note">of parenting time</div>
    </div>
    <div class="hstat">
      <div class="label">Went Pro Se</div>
      <div class="value red">{{ pro_se_pct }}%</div>
      <div class="note">{{ ran_out_pct }}% after running out of money</div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="secondary-stats">
    <div class="sstat"><div class="label">Submissions</div><div class="value">{{ total }}</div></div>
    <div class="sstat"><div class="label">Avg Children / Family</div><div class="value">{{ avg_children }}</div></div>
    <div class="sstat"><div class="label">Families Reporting Children</div><div class="value">{{ children_reporting }} of {{ total }}</div></div>
    <div class="sstat"><div class="label">Counties Represented</div><div class="value">{{ counties_represented }}</div></div>
  </div>

  <div class="megs-story">
    <div class="story-text">
      <h3>Why this report <span class="accent">exists.</span></h3>
      <p class="lede" style="color: rgba(255,255,255,0.92);">On January 29, 2024, I lost custody of all five of my children.</p>
      <ul class="bullets">
        <li>No trial.</li>
        <li>No questioning.</li>
        <li>No substantiated abuse.</li>
      </ul>
      <div class="divider"></div>
      <p>It took only a signature on an ex parte emergency order to erase a mother. I refused to disappear. I fought back, and built the Family Rights Registry so {{ state_name }} families — and families in every state — would stop being invisible to the data. This report is their record.</p>
      <div class="signoff">— Meg · StandWithMeg.com</div>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="page-foot">
    <div class="credit"><span class="star">★</span><span>A <strong>StandWithMeg.com</strong> Report · Family Rights Registry</span></div>
    <div class="pg">{{ state_name }} · {{ "%02d"|format(glance_page_number) }} / {{ total_pages }}</div>
  </div>
</section>

{# ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━ PAGE 3 — FINANCIAL ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━ #}
<section class="page">
  <div class="runhead">
    <div><span class="r-state">{{ state_name }}</span> · Family Court Data Report</div>
    <div class="r-page">Stand With Meg · {{ "%02d"|format(financial_page_number) }} / {{ total_pages }}</div>
  </div>

  <h2 class="section-head"><span class="num">{{ financial_section_num }}</span>The Cost of {{ state_name }} Family Court</h2>

  <p class="lede" style="margin-bottom: 18px;">Legal fees are the largest reported expense, but they are not the only one. Lost wages, evaluation costs, and reunification services compound the financial loss — pushing most families toward pro se representation once their savings run out.</p>

  <table class="expense-table">
    <thead>
      <tr>
        <th>Expense Category</th>
        <th class="num">Responses</th>
        <th class="num">Median</th>
        <th class="num">Mean</th>
        <th class="num">Total Reported</th>
      </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      {% for row in expense_rows %}
      <tr>
        <td class="headline">{{ row.label }}{% if row.footnote %} <span class="footnote-marker">{{ row.footnote }}</span>{% endif %}</td>
        <td class="num">{{ row.n }}</td>
        <td class="num">{{ row.median }}</td>
        <td class="num">{{ row.mean }}</td>
        <td class="num">{{ row.total }}</td>
      </tr>
      {% endfor %}
      <tr class="total-row">
        <td class="headline">Estimated All-Category Family Impact</td>
        <td class="num">—</td>
        <td class="num">{{ median_family_impact }}</td>
        <td class="num">—</td>
        <td class="num">—</td>
      </tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>


  <div class="footnote">
    <strong>Median vs. mean:</strong> Median is the middle reported amount, so it better reflects the typical reporting family when a few very large expenses appear. Mean is the average across reporting families and can be pulled higher by outliers. The estimated family impact sums the median reported amount in each expense category, so the headline reflects the all-category burden shown in the table.
  </div>

  {% if has_asset_footnote %}
  <div class="footnote">
    <strong>1. On asset loss:</strong> {{ asset_footnote_text }}
  </div>
  {% endif %}

  <div class="data-block" style="margin-top: 22px;">
    <h3>Lost Parenting Time · Months</h3>
    <div class="bar-row">
      <div class="bar-label">Median months lost</div>
      <div class="bar-track"><div class="bar-fill" style="width: {{ months_lost_median_bar }}%;"></div></div>
      <div class="bar-count">{{ months_lost_median }}</div>
      <div class="bar-pct">{{ months_lost_median_yrs }}</div>
    </div>
    <div class="bar-row">
      <div class="bar-label">Mean months lost</div>
      <div class="bar-track"><div class="bar-fill" style="width: {{ months_lost_mean_bar }}%;"></div></div>
      <div class="bar-count">{{ months_lost_mean }}</div>
      <div class="bar-pct">{{ months_lost_mean_yrs }}</div>
    </div>
    <div class="bar-row">
      <div class="bar-label">Total across all families</div>
      <div class="bar-track"><div class="bar-fill" style="width: 100%;"></div></div>
      <div class="bar-count">{{ months_lost_total }}</div>
      <div class="bar-pct">{{ months_lost_total_yrs }}</div>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="page-foot">
    <div class="credit"><span class="star">★</span><span>A <strong>StandWithMeg.com</strong> Report · Family Rights Registry</span></div>
    <div class="pg">{{ state_name }} · {{ "%02d"|format(financial_page_number) }} / {{ total_pages }}</div>
  </div>
</section>

{# ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━ PAGE 4 — WHO IS REPORTING + GEOGRAPHY + ALLEGATIONS ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━ #}
<section class="page">
  <div class="runhead">
    <div><span class="r-state">{{ state_name }}</span> · Family Court Data Report</div>
    <div class="r-page">Stand With Meg · {{ "%02d"|format(who_page_number) }} / {{ total_pages }}</div>
  </div>

  <h2 class="section-head"><span class="num">{{ who_section_num }}</span>Who Is Reporting · {{ state_name }}</h2>
  <p class="lede" style="margin-bottom: 14px; font-size: 13.5px;">Most families documenting in {{ state_name }} are currently active in, or recently closed out of, long-running cases. Nearly half have lost all contact with their children.</p>

  <div class="subsection">Case Status · System Affected</div>
  <div class="grid-2">
    <div class="data-block">
      <h3>Case Status</h3>
      {% for item in case_status %}
      <div class="bar-row"><div class="bar-label">{{ item.label }}</div><div class="bar-track"><div class="bar-fill" style="width: {{ item.bar_pct }}%;"></div></div><div class="bar-count">{{ item.count }}</div><div class="bar-pct">{{ item.pct }}%</div></div>
      {% endfor %}
    </div>

    <div class="data-block">
      <h3>System Affected</h3>
      {% for item in system %}
      <div class="bar-row"><div class="bar-label">{{ item.label }}</div><div class="bar-track"><div class="bar-fill" style="width: {{ item.bar_pct }}%;"></div></div><div class="bar-count">{{ item.count }}</div><div class="bar-pct">{{ item.pct }}%</div></div>
      {% endfor %}
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="subsection">Duration · Custody Outcomes</div>
  <div class="grid-2">
    <div class="data-block">
      <h3>Time in System</h3>
      {% for item in duration %}
      <div class="bar-row"><div class="bar-label">{{ item.label }}</div><div class="bar-track"><div class="bar-fill" style="width: {{ item.bar_pct }}%;"></div></div><div class="bar-count">{{ item.count }}</div><div class="bar-pct">{{ item.pct }}%</div></div>
      {% endfor %}
    </div>

    <div class="data-block">
      <h3>Custody Status</h3>
      {% for item in custody %}
      <div class="bar-row"><div class="bar-label">{{ item.label }}</div><div class="bar-track"><div class="bar-fill" style="width: {{ item.bar_pct }}%;"></div></div><div class="bar-count">{{ item.count }}</div><div class="bar-pct">{{ item.pct }}%</div></div>
      {% endfor %}
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="subsection">Geography · Allegations Reported</div>
  <div class="grid-2">
    <div class="data-block">
      <h3>Top Counties</h3>
      {% for item in counties %}
      <div class="bar-row"><div class="bar-label">{{ item.label }}</div><div class="bar-track"><div class="bar-fill" style="width: {{ item.bar_pct }}%;"></div></div><div class="bar-count">{{ item.count }}</div><div class="bar-pct">{{ item.pct }}%</div></div>
      {% endfor %}
    </div>

    <div class="data-block">
      <h3>Top Allegations Reported</h3>
      {% for item in allegations %}
      <div class="bar-row"><div class="bar-label">{{ item.label }}</div><div class="bar-track"><div class="bar-fill" style="width: {{ item.bar_pct }}%;"></div></div><div class="bar-count">{{ item.count }}</div><div class="bar-pct">{{ item.pct }}%</div></div>
      {% endfor %}
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="page-foot">
    <div class="credit"><span class="star">★</span><span>A <strong>StandWithMeg.com</strong> Report · Family Rights Registry</span></div>
    <div class="pg">{{ state_name }} · {{ "%02d"|format(who_page_number) }} / {{ total_pages }}</div>
  </div>
</section>


{# ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━ PARENT VOICES ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━ #}
{% for voice_page in voice_pages %}
<section class="page">
  <div class="runhead">
    <div><span class="r-state">{{ state_name }}</span> · Family Court Data Report</div>
    <div class="r-page">Stand With Meg · {{ "%02d"|format(voices_start_page + loop.index0) }} / {{ total_pages }}</div>
  </div>

  {% if loop.first %}
  <h2 class="section-head"><span class="num">{{ voices_section_num }}</span>Parent Voices — {{ state_name }}</h2>
  <p class="lede" style="margin-bottom: 18px;">Selected voice excerpts appear here for readability. Every approved, shareable {{ state_name }} comment is printed in full in the appendix that follows.</p>
  {% else %}
  <h2 class="section-head"><span class="num">{{ voices_section_num }}</span>Parent Voices, continued</h2>
  {% endif %}

  {% if voice_page.pullquote %}
  <div class="pullquote">
    <span class="mark">"</span>
    <blockquote>{{ voice_page.pullquote.quote }}</blockquote>
    <cite>— {{ voice_page.pullquote.attribution }}</cite>
  </div>
  {% endif %}

  {% if loop.first and allegation_quote %}
  <div class="subsection" style="color: var(--crimson); border-bottom-color: rgba(185,28,28,0.35); margin-top: 18px;">On the Reported Allegations</div>
  <div class="voice-card" style="margin-bottom: 14px;">
    <blockquote>{{ allegation_quote.quote }}</blockquote>
    <cite>— {{ allegation_quote.attribution }}</cite>
  </div>
  <div class="subsection">More Voices from {{ state_name }}</div>
  {% endif %}

  <div class="voices-grid">
    {% for v in voice_page.cards %}
    <div class="voice-card">
      <blockquote>{{ v.quote }}</blockquote>
      <cite>— {{ v.attribution }}</cite>
    </div>
    {% endfor %}
  </div>

  {% if loop.last %}
  <p class="caption" style="margin-top: 16px; text-align: center;">
    {{ total_publishable_quotes }} {{ state_name }} parents submitted approved, shareable comments. {{ quotes_shown }} selected excerpts appear here; the full comments begin on the next page.
  </p>
  {% endif %}
  <div class="page-foot">
    <div class="credit"><span class="star">★</span><span>A <strong>StandWithMeg.com</strong> Report · Family Rights Registry</span></div>
    <div class="pg">{{ state_name }} · {{ "%02d"|format(voices_start_page + loop.index0) }} / {{ total_pages }}</div>
  </div>
</section>
{% endfor %}

{# ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━ FULL PARENT COMMENTS APPENDIX ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━ #}
{% for quote_page in full_comment_pages %}
<section class="page">
  <div class="runhead">
    <div><span class="r-state">{{ state_name }}</span> · Family Court Data Report</div>
    <div class="r-page">Stand With Meg · {{ "%02d"|format(full_comments_start_page + loop.index0) }} / {{ total_pages }}</div>
  </div>

  {% if loop.first %}
  <h2 class="section-head"><span class="num">{{ full_comments_section_num }}</span>Full Parent Comments — {{ state_name }}</h2>
  <p class="lede" style="margin-bottom: 14px;">The comments below are the full approved, publicly shareable survey comments from {{ state_name }} families. Data-only and do-not-share submissions are excluded from this public appendix.</p>
  {% else %}
  <h2 class="section-head"><span class="num">{{ full_comments_section_num }}</span>Full Parent Comments, continued</h2>
  {% endif %}

  <div class="full-comments-list">
    {% for v in quote_page.cards %}
    <div class="full-comment-card">
      <blockquote>{{ v.quote }}</blockquote>
      <cite>— {{ v.attribution }}</cite>
    </div>
    {% endfor %}
  </div>

  {% if loop.last %}
  <p class="caption" style="margin-top: 12px; text-align: center;">
    {{ full_comments_total }} full approved {{ state_name }} comments are included in this appendix.
  </p>
  {% endif %}

  <div class="page-foot">
    <div class="credit"><span class="star">★</span><span>A <strong>StandWithMeg.com</strong> Report · Family Rights Registry</span></div>
    <div class="pg">{{ state_name }} · {{ "%02d"|format(full_comments_start_page + loop.index0) }} / {{ total_pages }}</div>
  </div>
</section>
{% endfor %}

{# ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━ LAST PAGE — METHODOLOGY / CLOSING ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━ #}
<section class="page">
  <div class="runhead">
    <div><span class="r-state">{{ state_name }}</span> · Family Court Data Report</div>
    <div class="r-page">Stand With Meg · {{ "%02d"|format(methodology_page_number) }} / {{ total_pages }}</div>
  </div>

  <h2 class="section-head"><span class="num">{{ methodology_section_num }}</span>How to Read This Report</h2>

  <div class="grid-2">
    <div>
      <h3 style="font-family: var(--font-display); text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.09em; font-weight: 600; font-size: 12px; color: var(--navy); margin: 0 0 10px;">What this is</h3>
      <p class="body-text">The Family Rights Registry is a national, parent-reported data collection run by Stand With Meg. Every figure in this {{ state_name }} report comes from {{ state_name }} respondents who voluntarily submitted survey entries about their experience inside family court and/or CPS.</p>
      <p class="body-text" style="margin-top: 10px;">This report is built to help families, advocates, reporters, and legislators see the patterns emerging in {{ state_name }} — not to replace formal research, and not to name individual judges or counties as responsible parties.</p>
    </div>
    <div>
      <h3 style="font-family: var(--font-display); text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.09em; font-weight: 600; font-size: 12px; color: var(--navy); margin: 0 0 10px;">What it isn't</h3>
      <p class="body-text">This is not a representative sample. Respondents self-select. The {{ total }} {{ state_name }} families reporting here are not the universe of {{ state_name }} families in court — they are the families who found the survey, trusted it enough to submit, and told us what happened to them.</p>
      <p class="body-text" style="margin-top: 10px;">Financial figures are self-reported. We flag outliers and report medians when means are distorted (see page 3, note 1). The family-impact headline is an all-category estimate based on category medians. Quotes are minimally edited.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="methodology">
    <h3>Methodology · Family Rights Registry</h3>
    <p>Data in this report was collected April 2024 – {{ report_month_year }} through standwithmeg.com/family-rights-survey. Submissions are timestamped. Duplicate-submission heuristics use normalized email + location, with direct survey rows preferred over legacy rows and the newest row retained within each source. Categorical responses from multi-select and short-answer fields are normalized monthly.</p>
    <p>When a respondent's financial entry differs from the population by more than three standard deviations, the mean is suppressed and only the median is reported. Lost-wage, attorney-fee, and asset-loss entries are self-reported and not corroborated against tax records or court filings.</p>
    <p>Geographic reporting uses the county field as submitted, with light normalization (e.g. "Butte silverbow" → "Butte–Silver Bow"). Quotes carry one of three public permission states: <em>Anonymous</em>, <em>First-name only</em>, or <em>Full attribution with consent to public use</em>. Court actor names appear only after {{ court_actor_threshold }} independent families name the same actor.</p>
    <div class="site">standwithmeg.com · courage to stand, power to change</div>
  </div>

  <div style="margin-top: 24px; padding-top: 16px; border-top: 2px solid var(--navy);">
    <div class="eyebrow" style="margin-bottom: 8px;">About this report</div>
    <p class="body-text" style="margin: 0 0 6px;">This report is based on self-reported survey submissions collected by Stand With Meg. Counts and categories reflect responses available at the time this packet was generated.</p>
    <p class="body-text" style="margin: 0 0 10px;">This report is for informational and advocacy use only, not legal advice or an official government record.</p>
    <div style="font-family: var(--font-display); text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.14em; font-size: 11px; color: var(--crimson); font-weight: 600;">StandWithMeg.com <span style="color: var(--navy); font-weight: 400;">|</span> <span style="color: var(--navy);">Courage to Stand, Power to Change.</span></div>
  </div>
  <div class="page-foot">
    <div class="credit"><span class="star">★</span><span>A <strong>StandWithMeg.com</strong> Report · Family Rights Registry</span></div>
    <div class="pg">{{ state_name }} · {{ "%02d"|format(methodology_page_number) }} / {{ total_pages }}</div>
  </div>
</section>

</body>
</html>
